 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nTable cell grid_span property cannot be set after removal of setter\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen trying to set the grid_span property on table cells, the operation fails because the setter method has been removed. This breaks functionality for merging table cells that need to span multiple columns.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom docx import Document\nfrom docx.oxml.table import CT_TcPr\n\n# Create a document with a table\ndoc = Document()\ntable = doc.add_table(rows=2, cols=3)\n\n# Get the first cell and try to set its grid span\ncell = table.cell(0, 0)\ntc_pr = cell._tc.get_or_add_tcPr()\n\n# This should work but fails\ntc_pr.grid_span = 2\n```\n\nThe above code raises an AttributeError because the grid_span setter is no longer available, even though the getter still exists.\n\n#### Expected Behavior\n\nSetting `tc_pr.grid_span = 2` should create the appropriate gridSpan element with val=2 to make the cell span across 2 columns.\n\n#### Actual Behavior\n\nAttributeError is raised when trying to assign to the grid_span property since only the getter exists.\n</issue>\n",
